## Skill routing

Project skills live in `.cursor/skills/` (Cursor) and `.agents/skills/` (Antigravity). **Pick one primary skill per turn** unless the user asks for a staged multi-pass review.

| Intent | Skill | Use when |
|--------|-------|----------|
| Session bootstrap | `using-skills` | Starting work; unsure which skill applies |
| Product/copy context | `product-context` | Positioning, audience, messaging, ICP |
| New feature design | `brainstorming` | Before creative work or new behavior |
| Bugs / failures | `systematic-debugging` | Errors, test failures, unexpected behavior |
| Claiming done | `verification-before-completion` | Before saying fixed, complete, or passing |
| UI polish | `frontend-polish` | Layout, spacing, hierarchy, Tailwind cleanup |
| Marketing copy | `copywriting` | Headlines, landing copy, CTAs |
| SEO review | `seo-audit` | Meta, structure, on-page SEO |

**Do not** load `frontend-polish` and `copywriting` for the same UI pass unless staged. **Do** chain `brainstorming` → implementation → `verification-before-completion`.

Announce which skill you are applying in one short sentence.
